ine on Venkatanarayana Road, T. Nagar — one of two Sharadhamba temples on this list within about a kilometre of each other, this one and the Kripa Shankari Street shrine in neighbouring West Mambalam.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":9.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mambalam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"344e37b2-1639-4748-b2a1-6bc5aba137c1","name":"Vimleshwar Temple","deity":"Shiva as Vimaleshwar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Goa","district":"Kushavati","town":"Rivona","latitude":15.165,"longitude":74.107,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kushavati River","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:13:52.370722+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple in Rivona village, Sanguem taluka, Goa, where Shiva is worshipped as Vimaleshwar in the form of a Shivalinga regarded as self-manifested (swayambhu). The Prabhu Dessai family of Rivona and the Daivajna Brahmins with the Rivonkar or Revankar surname are its Mahajans.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Goa International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":38,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Balli railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":9.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Vimleshwar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"346ce5b5-8482-44d9-bfba-57710033d4d4","name":"Vishnupad Temple, Gaya","deity":"Vishnu","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Gaya","town":"Gaya","latitude":24.7955,"longitude":85.0002,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Falgu","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":"Sep–Oct for Pitru Paksha, when pind daan rites peak; Oct–Feb otherwise.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:57:28.972216+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built in its present form in 1787 under the patronage of Maharani Ahilyabai Holkar, on a site with a documented history reaching back to the Gupta era. The temple's sanctum holds a 40-cm footprint said to be Vishnu's own, set into basalt rock. Tradition holds the demon Gayasura won a boon that anyone who saw him would attain moksha; Vishnu pinned him underground with his foot to stop this, leaving the footprint, and granted Gayasura's request that people be able to free their ancestors through pind daan offered here — making Gaya one of the principal sites in India for that rite.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"विष्णुपद मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":"06:00:00","morning_closes_at":"12:00:00","evening_opens_at":"16:00:00","evening_closes_at":"20:00:00","timings_notes":"Open every day including public holidays; some sources report a longer midday closure (up to 4pm).","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name