me":"Gomti (confluence with the Arabian Sea)","river_distance_km":0.4,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Mar. Easily combined with the Dwarkadhish temple and Nageshwar Jyotirlinga.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T13:44:40.752775+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"The western Amnaya peetham, associated with the Sama Veda. Its mahavakya is Tattvamasi — \"thou art that\" — and it is traditionally held to have been entrusted by Adi Shankaracharya to his disciple Hastamalaka.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"द्वारका शारदा पीठम्","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Porbandar","nearest_airport_distance_km":96.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Dwarka railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"368bac21-b688-45c6-860a-b30dc2ea4830","name":"Kodandarama Temple, Gollala Mamidada","deity":"Rama","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Kakinada","town":"Gollala Mamidada","latitude":16.93822,"longitude":82.07378,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Tulyabhaga (Antharvahini), a tributary of the Godavari","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:56.940052+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Rama temple at Gollala Mamidada in Kakinada district, on the Tulyabhaga, a Godavari tributary. Construction began in 1889 with a small shrine, a larger temple followed in 1939, and the two tall gopurams date to 1948-58. Known as the Little Bhadrachalam, its main festival is Sri Rama Navami with an annual wedding ceremony.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Rajahmundry Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":33.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bikkavolu railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Kodandarama Temple, Gollala Mamidada), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":20},{"id":"3757c330-2768-459a-9f26-6b081805362e","name":"Jagannath Temple, Digha","deity":"Jagannath with Balarama and Subhadra","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Purba Medinipur","town":"Digha","latitude":21.62301,"longitude":87.49236,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Subarnarekha River","river_distance_km":14.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A modern temple in Digha enshrining Jagannath, a form of Vishnu, with Balarama and Subhadra. It was built as a replica of the Jagannath Temple in Puri, announced in 2018, begun in 2022 and inaugurated on 30 April 2025 after a consecration ceremony.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":151.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Digha railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Jagannath Temple, Digha), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Replica of Puri Jagannath Temple","construction_century":21},{"id":"378cea44-6116-438f-808b-2c41ff0680fe","name":"Vishnu Temple, Ganpatganj","deity":"Vishnu","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Supaul","town":"Raghopur","latitude":26.28389,"longitude":86.82889,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Koshi River","river_distance_km":6.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A modern Vishnu temple at Ganpatganj in Supaul, Bihar, also called Vishnudham or Sri Varadraja Perumal Devasthanam. It stands beside National Highway 131 on about 15 acres. Dr. Pawan Kumar Mallik, founder of the managing trust, laid its foundation stone in 2004, and construction finished in 2014.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Purnea Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":81.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Raghopur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Vishnu Temple, Ganpatganj), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"37e3726f-f452-440d-b39e-1833346c7f45","name":"Maa Manasa Temple, Jakpur","deity":"Manasa","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Paschim Medinipur","town":"Narayangarh","latitude":22.20347,"longitude":87.41317,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kaliaghai River","river_distance_km":5.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Hindu temple at Jakpur near Kharagpur dedicated to Maa Manasa, notable for having no roof. The present building dates from a 2012 rebuilding. Devotees gather on Saturdays and Tuesdays, with a special puja on the third Tuesday of the Bengali month of Chaitra.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":117.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Narayangarh railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Maa Manasa Temple, Jakpur), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"3810f601-c139-45db-8154-9d6be3ddde02","name":"Amarnath Cave Temple","deity":"Shiva (ice lingam)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Jammu and Kashmir","district":"Anantnag","town":"Amarnath","latitude":34.2104,"longitude":75.5,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Langars run by NGOs and the Shri Amarnath Shrine Board along the yatra route and near the cave — entirely free, seasonal (yatra months only)","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0,"nearest_river_name":"Sind River","river_distance_km":2,"best_season_notes":"Accessible only during the official Amarnath Yatra window, typically late June to August — otherwise snowbound and closed.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition holds that Shiva revealed the secret of immortality (Amar Katha) to Parvati in this remote Himalayan cave, and that a pair of pigeons overheard it and became immortal themselves — pilgrims still report sighting a pair of doves near the cave. The ice lingam (a naturally forming stalagmite) that appears each year, waxing and waning with the moon, is worshipped as a swayambhu (self-manifest) form of Shiva.","etiquette_notes":"Accessible only by trekking or pony/palanquin during the official Amarnath Yatra window (typically late June to August), and only with the mandatory permit obtained in advance along with a medical fitness certificate — this is a genuine high-altitude trek, not a casual visit.","native_name":"अमरनाथ गुफा मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Cave open for darshan roughly 6am–4pm during the yatra window itself. The season is strictly limited to about 40–60 days each summer (from Vyas Purnima to Shravan Purnima on the lunar calendar), typically falling within July–August — exact dates are fixed annually by the Shri Amarnathji Shrine Board, not a fixed calendar range.","accessibility_notes":"Only reachable on foot or by pony/palanquin during the official Amarnath Yatra window, over a genuinely difficult multi-day high-altitude trek (from either the Pahalgam or Baltal route). Not accessible to wheelchair users or anyone without a mandatory medical fitness certificate.","nearest_airport_name":"Srinagar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":93,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Jammu Tawi","nearest_railway_distance_km":315,"emergency_contact_notes":"Dial 112 for all-India police/medical/fire emergency services. Registration with the Shri Amarnathji Shrine Board is mandatory before the yatra, including a medical fitness certificate — this registration process is also how the Board and J&K authorities track and assist pilgrims on the route. Base camps at Pahalgam and Baltal have medical posts along the trek.","sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition, not a single classical Sanskrit text","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"3835a76f-2d84-4fba-8d38-5bb38d7465ea","name":"Nuggikeri Hanuman Temple","deity":"Hanuman","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Dharwad","town":"Nuggikeri","latitude":15.41307,"longitude":75.00543,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Bedti nala River","river_distance_km":4.4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A well-known old temple at Nuggikeri in Dharwad, on the airport road about 18 km from central Hubli. Hanuman is the presiding deity, and the complex also houses shrines to Rama, Shiva, Saraswati, Durga, Santoshimata, Venugopala Swamy and Jagannath. It draws large crowds on Saturdays and on Hanuman Jayanti.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Hubballi Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":9.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Dharwad railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Nuggikeri Hanuman Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"38c89d1c-defd-499a-b6fe-f8564f3d0d19","name":"Sundaravarada Perumal temple","deity":"Vishnu as Sundaravarada Perumal","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tamil Nadu","town":"Uttiramerur","latitude":12.61472,"longitude":79.755,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cheyyar River","river_distance_km":8.4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:38.937899+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Vishnu temple in Uthiramerur, originally Pallava work with later additions from Chola, Pandya, Vijayanagara and Nayak rulers. Unusually, it has three sanctums in a two-tiered structure. According to tradition, Vishnu appeared here for the Pandava princes. It follows the Vadakalai tradition and has a five-tiered gopuram.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":61.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Karunguzhi railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":19.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Sundaravarada Perumal temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"38df2675-1fbe-4b10-af1d-46ed74c36f22","name":"Devanathaswamy temple, Thiruvanthipuram","deity":"Vishnu as Devanatha with Lakshmi as Hemabhujavalli","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Cuddalore","town":"Thiruvandhipuram","latitude":11.74481,"longitude":79.70899,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Gadilam River","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T10:59:23.880063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Dravidian-style Vishnu temple near Cuddalore, Tamil Nadu, and one of the 108 Divya Desams praised by the Alvars. It is noted for a hilltop shrine to Hayagriva. The present form is thought to date to the Medieval Cholas, with later Pandya, Hoysala and Vijayanagara additions, and about fifty inscriptions survive.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Neyveli Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":24.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruppadirippuliyur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Devanathaswamy temple, Thiruvanthipuram), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"390d9176-6bda-4d4d-a3e1-7ceb58e811c0","name":"Shree Betal temple","deity":"Betal, a Bhairava form of Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Goa","district":"North Goa","town":"Amona","latitude":15.53333,"longitude":73.98333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cudnem River","river_distance_km":0.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:11.054915+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple in Amona village, Bicholim taluk, where Betal is worshipped as a warrior form of Bhairava and as the village guardian deity. The standing idol is carried on horseback through the village at festivals. The temple also has a Shiva pindi and its attendant gana, and a well stands 50 metres away.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Goa International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":23.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Karmali railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shree Betal temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"3923cd9d-dc45-46a3-9c49-52e7fdba6713","name":"Kalika Mata Temple, Chittorgarh Fort","deity":"Kalika Mata (Devi)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Chittorgarh","town":"Chittorgarh","latitude":24.8829,"longitude":74.6467,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Gambhiri River","river_distance_km":1.4,"best_season_notes":"Sep–Oct for Navaratri; otherwise Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T18:27:49.795249+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Originally an 8th-century Surya (sun) temple built by Bappa Rawal, damaged in Alauddin Khalji’s 1303 sack of Chittorgarh Fort, and rededicated to the goddess Kalika (also known locally as Chittodeshwari) after Rana Hamir installed her idol here in the 14th century. The Mewar ruler Maharana Lakshman Singh is credited with lighting an eternal flame (Akhanda Jyoti) here that tradition holds has burned ever since.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"कालिका माता मंदिर, चित्तौड़गढ़","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Maharana Pratap Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":81,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chittaurgarh Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":8},{"id":"39d842d8-5365-4f46-a91a-97f06934d227","name":"Bhavanarayana Temple, Sarpavaram","deity":"Vishnu as Bhavanarayana","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Kakinada","town":"Yetimoga","latitude":16.95,"longitude":82.25,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Koringa River","river_distance_km":9.4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:11.054915+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A historic Vishnu temple in Sarpavaram, about 5 km from Kakinada, and a state-protected monument. Its earliest inscription is dated 1073 CE, suggesting the temple is older. It was repaired and rebuilt over the centuries under successive rulers and is mentioned in 15th-century Telugu works by Srinatha.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Rajahmundry Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":49.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kakinada Port railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Bhavanarayana Temple, Sarpavaram), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":11},{"id":"39eb4bd6-c3e2-4393-baa2-0f2fa6f34f24","name":"Mangaladevi Temple, Mangaluru","deity":"Mangaladevi (Shakti)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Dakshina Kannada","town":"Bolara, Mangaluru","latitude":12.8491,"longitude":74.8432,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Netravati River","river_distance_km":1.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T09:54:32.209521+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"About 3 km southwest of the city centre, dedicated to Shakti as Mangaladevi, the presiding deity from whom the city takes its name. Tradition says it was built in the 9th century by the Alupa king Kundavarman under the patronage of Matsyendranath; another account credits Parashurama, with Kundavarman later expanding it. The deity sits in the central shrine, with surrounding shrines for other deities. It is run by trustees.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Open daily 6 am–1 pm and 4 pm–8:30 pm (per Wikipedia; confirm locally before travelling).","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mangalore International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":12.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mangaluru Central railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Mangaladevi Temple)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":9},{"id":"3a51bfb1-3f2f-47ff-bf8d-247c8ddb519e","name":"Shri Laxminarayan Temple, Kolkata","deity":"Lakshmi Narayana","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Kolkata","town":"Kolkata","latitude":22.53332,"longitude":88.35378,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adi Ganga River","river_distance_km":1.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T10:59:23.880063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple on Sarat Bose Road in Bhawanipur, Kolkata, set up in 1952 by the local Gujarati Vaishnav community. The main sanctum holds Lakshmi Narayana, Rama, Sita and Lakshmana and a Shiva linga, with Hanuman and Ganesha in side shrines. A charitable trust manages it, and the complex includes a dharamshala and hall.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":16.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Park Circus railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shri Laxminarayan Temple, Kolkata), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":20},{"id":"3a7b4b9b-2259-462f-90e9-ed1685c3366d","name":"Sheetla Mata Mandir, Gurugram","deity":"Sheetla Devi — goddess of protection from smallpox and fevers, and the kuldevi (patron goddess) of Gurugram; local tradition identifies her with Kripi, wife of Dronacharya from the Mahabharata","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Haryana","district":"Gurugram","town":"Gurugram","latitude":28.4783,"longitude":77.0305,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"Navratri (both Chaitra and Ashvin) is the major season; Chaitra-month Mondays are especially busy. A week-long fair falls in Ashadha/Sawan, alongside an annual \"Gardabh Mela\" (donkey fair) distinctive to this site.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T19:09:34.948917+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-22T19:09:34.948917+00:00","sthala_purana":"Sources genuinely disagree on the temple's origin, and both are recorded here rather than one being picked silently: one tradition holds the goddess was a real woman, Kripi, devoted to nursing smallpox-afflicted children, with villagers building a shrine after her death; a separate mythological framing (repeated on the temple's own Wikipedia page) dates the site to \"1000 AD\" tied to Yudhishthira in the Dvapara Yuga; a third, tourism-sourced account credits an 18th-century Jat king, Jawahar Singh of Bharatpur, with building the temple to commemorate a military victory.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Per tourism sources, not an official schedule: roughly 5am–12pm and 4–9pm.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Indira Gandhi International Airport, Delhi","nearest_airport_distance_km":17,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Gurugram Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local tradition (multiple conflicting accounts); no single documented founding date","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"3aef0c32-a781-4b62-b422-0e99012895ce","name":"Sthaneshwar Mahadev Temple","deity":"Shiva as Mahadev","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Haryana","district":"Kurukshetra","town":"Kurukshetra","latitude":29.981,"longitude":76.828,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:47.875457+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient Shiva temple in old Kurukshetra, Haryana. According to tradition, the Pandavas and Krishna prayed to Shiva here and received his blessing for victory in the Mahabharata war. A gurdwara beside it marks where the ninth Sikh Guru, Tegh Bahadur, stayed.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Sarsawa Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":55.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Thanesar City railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.6,"emer