approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:57:28.972216+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built by the Pallava king Narasimhavarman I in the 8th century, with a temple inscription dated 808 CE. Krishna is worshipped here as Parthasarathy, \"charioteer of Partha (Arjuna),\" in a rare nine-foot standing form with a moustache, carrying a conch but — by vow to stay unarmed in that role — no discus. One of the 108 Divya Desams, it is unusual for depicting Krishna alongside Rukmini, Balarama, Satyaki, Pradyumna, and Aniruddha together.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"பார்த்தசாரதி கோயில்","morning_opens_at":"06:00:00","morning_closes_at":"12:00:00","evening_opens_at":"16:00:00","evening_closes_at":"21:00:00","timings_notes":"Opens earlier (5:30am) on Saturdays and stays open till 10pm that day.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":13.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Thiruvallikeni railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"44f19ff5-9f32-4ece-8771-143514d3cb97","name":"Mundeshwari Temple","deity":"Durga as Mundeshwari, with Shiva","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Kaimur","town":"Bhagwanpur","latitude":24.9834,"longitude":83.56469,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Son","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:53.924452+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"A hilltop temple at Ramgarh on the Kaimur plateau near the Son river in Bihar, protected by the ASI since 1915. Claims of a 108 CE date make it the oldest functioning temple, but historians say the surviving architecture is no older than the 6th to 7th century and the octagonal shrine may be much later.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Lal Bahadur Shastri International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":87.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Muthani railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":20.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Mundeshwari Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Octagonal shrine","construction_century":7}]$rtam$::jsonb)
